      "observation": "# Duration format\n\nA duration is one or more `<number><unit>` pairs, concatenated with no\nseparator. Units are:\n\n| unit | meaning | seconds |\n|------|---------|---------|\n| `d`  | days    | 86400   |\n| `h`  | hours   | 3600    |\n| `m`  | minutes | 60      |\n| `s`  | seconds | 1       |\n\n`parse_duration` returns the total number of seconds.\n\n## Fractional values\n\nNumbers may be fractional. The total is computed exactly and rounded to\nthe nearest whole second. **`1.5h` is 5400 seconds**, not 3600 — a\nfractional value is not truncated to whole units.\n\nExamples: `45s` -> 45, `2h` -> 7200, `1h30m` -> 5400, `2d` -> 172800,\n`0.5h` -> 1800, `1.5h` -> 5400, `2.5m` -> 150.\n\nUnits may appear in any combination. A value may exceed the natural\nrange of its unit (`90m` is 5400 seconds).\n",
